PeaBrain trainable model — design record (branch feat/model-arena).
Companion to BUILD (MCP engine). Stages: 1 arena+save/load, 2 AVX2/FMA
FP32 engine, 3 backprop+validation, 4 VNNI/INT8(+INT4/FP16) inference,
5 GPU feasibility probe, 6 GPU only if proven. Prototype lives in model/
standalone; MCP tools (model_init/train/predict/save/load/status) wire up
only after Stage 3 is green. Live peabrain.db is never touched by tests.

ARENA: mmap 4GiB MAP_PRIVATE|MAP_ANONYMOUS|MAP_NORESERVE (reserve address
space, commit on demand). Internal align = max(request,4096) so mincore
accounting is exact per region. Bump allocator + 64-entry region table
{tag,off,size,align}; mark/reset for load rollback. allocated = acur
high-water; committed = mincore residency sum over regions.

PBMD v1 (LE): hdr 64B {magic 'PBMD', ver=1, arch=1(x86-64/AVX2+FMA base),
flags, count, rsv, step u64, payload_bytes u64, table_crc FNV64, payload_crc
FNV64, rsv} + count*32B table {tag,aren_off,size,data_crc FNV64} + payload
(regions concatenated in table order). Validate: magic/ver/arch, count<=64,
file_size == 64+count*32+payload_bytes, table_crc, per-region data_crc,
payload_crc — in that order, before touching live regions.
SAVE: tmp sibling (O_CREAT|O_EXCL), two passes (hash then write), looped
writes, fsync file, renameat over target, fsync dir. Any failure unlinks tmp;
a valid checkpoint is never replaced by a partial one.
LOAD: fstat size check, stream regions into staging allocs from a saved mark,
verify each hash; any failure rolls back to the mark — current model survives.
Reject: bad magic/version/arch/count, short file, hash mismatch, alloc fail.

ENGINE (Stage 2): row-major FP32. AVX2/FMA primary (vbroadcastss + vfmadd231ps
outer-product micro-kernel, 8-wide), scalar reference kernel, agreement test
vs independent reference within 1e-5 relative. Runtime CPUID: AVX2/FMA
required for fast path (else reference + warn in model_status); AVX_VNNI
(VEX vpdpbusd) for Stage 4 INT8; AVX-512 masses detect-and-skip (absent here).
Same PBMD format for all backends (quant params ride in step/meta later).

TRAINING (Stage 3): MLP fwd (matmul+bias+act), MSE loss, backprop, SGD.
Prove: unknown linear map first, then f(x,y)=3x^2-2y+1. Metrics: train loss
+ held-out validation error must both fall (no memorisation). Save/resume:
step counter + weights round-trip exactly; predictions identical post-load.

BUILD: mlp_core.asm + mlp_data.asm splice onto arena infra (which carries
the PBMD save/load + arena alloc + prints; arena's own _start self-test is
excluded from the splice):
  python3 -c "a=open('arena.asm').read();
  out=a[:a.index('; ---- self-test ----')]+open('mlp_core.asm').read()+chr(10)+a[a.index('segment readable writeable'):]+chr(10)+open('mlp_data.asm').read();
  open('mlp.asm','w').write(out)"
  fasm mlp.asm /tmp/mlp && /tmp/mlp            (train)
  /tmp/mlp resume                               (restart: load, verify, resume)
mlp.asm is GENERATED (not committed); mlp_core/mlp_data are the sources.

STAGE 3 RESULTS (2026-11-04, all strict asserts green, exit 0):
- MICRO (hand N=1 H=1 linear): loss 10.24 exact, grads [25.6,38.4,12.8,
  11.84,6.4] all rel<1e-5 vs hand computation. Proves fwd+backprop exactly.
- LINEAR 2->8->1 (t=2.5x-1.7y+0.8, init independent): 9.3 -> 2e-8 train,
  held matches, 8 unseen points maxerr-e6=0 (bit-exact predictions).
- GRADCHECK (H=4 N=8, central diff eps=1e-2): linear AND leaky both strict:
  all params rel<1e-3 except ONE (W1[2], absdiff 4.4e-5) passing via the
  documented 1e-4 abs floor (FP32 cancellation on small grads). NaN-safe
  comparisons; exact param-restore check (loss bits identical after).
  ReLU kink safety: deterministic reseed (bounded 16) keeps all |z+b1| >
  0.05; perturbation shifts z by <=0.02, so crossing is impossible.
  Two real bugs caught: (1) backward ReLU gate MUST test the biased sum
  z+b1, not raw z (found via margin anomalies); (2) margin scan must also
  use z+b1 (it scanned raw Z1 and could never pass with b1=2.0).
- NONLINEAR 2->16->1 leaky-ReLU(0.01), full-batch warmup replaced by
  deterministic cyclic minibatches (B=16, slice = f(mstep), bit-exact
  across save/resume): INIT 61.6/80.8 -> S1 20000 @lr0.05 -> S2 20000
  @lr0.01 -> train 0.0079 / held 0.0109 (~8000x down, gap 1.4x, no
  memorisation). Chosen over plain-ReLU (dead units trapped lr=0.05 at
  0.24) and over full-batch (stuck at 0.019).
- PERSISTENCE: 8 PBMD regions (W1,b1,W2,b2 + 4 momentum velocities) +
  step counter. Restart test: RESUME block == SAVE block and RFINAL ==
  FINAL block, byte-identical (diff clean): reload fidelity + continued
  training bit-exact vs uninterrupted.
- Determinism: fixed LCG seeds everywhere; three consecutive full runs
  bit-identical (md5). Tolerances: micro 1e-5, grad rel 1e-3 + abs floor
  1e-4, linear 1e-6/1e-3-unseen, nonlinear train<0.015 held<0.02
  improve>=100x gap<5x. ASLR-independent (setarch -R identical).
- init_w/gendata cover [-1,0) not [-1,1) (shr 41 keeps 23 bits; comments
  said [0,2) — off by 2x; harmless here, noted for training quality).
  Same quirk exists in mat.asm (left as-is: distribution-independent
  proofs there).
- Future: H=32 capacity, target normalisation, per-param eps, INT4/FP16
  (Stage 4), GPU probe (Stage 5). Live peabrain.db never touched.

QUANT (Stage 4): INT8 symmetric per-tensor scale (+INT4 nibble packing and
FP16 storage evaluated where they win); inference-only, training stays FP32;
tolerance documented vs FP32. VNNI vpdpbusd sdot; scalar dequant reference.

STAGE 4 RESULTS (2026-11-04, ALL PASS, exit 0; model/quant.asm standalone):
Scheme (affine, documented in quant.asm header): X_q uint8 asymmetric
(sx,zx), W_q int8 symmetric (sw, zp=0), int32 accumulate (no overflow:
K<=256 -> 8.3M << 2^31), Y = sx*sw*(acc - zx*colsum) + b_fp32, colsum
precomputed; K padded to x4 (pad A=zx, W=0: exactly 0). Hidden A1
requantised (calibrated sa/za); biases stay FP32. Test net 2->16->1
leaky-ReLU with He-scale weights (the representative PeaBrain-init case),
64 inputs; scales/zp printed (sx=0.015661/zx=127, sa=0.010967/za=3).
- VNNI acc == scalar acc BIT-EXACT (1024B A1q + 64 preds, 0 mismatches).
  Methodology: both paths share lane_out/out2_finish (identical FP op
  order), so exactness holds by construction; padding verified (pad=0).
- INT8 vs independent FP32-scalar reference: maxabs 0.0124, meanabs
  0.0048. Tolerance 0.05 (4x measured; every real bug seen produced
  >=0.18). A wild-+-2-weight stress net measured 0.18 (documented, not
  asserted: per-tensor INT8 on wide ranges is honest there).
- 256^3 bench: scalar-INT8 == VNNI-INT8 bit-exact (65536 dwords, 0
  mismatches); scalar 12-15ms vs VNNI 1ms (12-15x) vs FP32-AVX2 2ms
  (VNNI-INT8 2x our best FP32). B packed once into 4x8 blocks (standard).
- Backend: CPUID AVX_VNNI = leaf7/subleaf1 EAX b4 (VEX); scalar fallback
  still proves the quant math. AVX-512 masses detect-and-skip (absent).
- VEX ENCODING GOTCHA (recorded so nobody repeats it): FASM 1.73 emits
  EVEX vpdpbusd (62...), which #UDs on this AVX-VNNI-only CPU. Hand-encoded
  VEX.128.66.0F38 C4 E3->E2 79 50 D1 (map byte is 0xE2=0F38, NOT 0xE3=0F3A;
  first attempt faulted). Macro vdpbd (fixed dest=xmm2,src=xmm0,src=xmm1);
  verified live (1+4+9+16=30 test).
- Bugs caught: (1) FP32-ref W1 row-1 stride 32*4 vs 16*4 (read b1f as
  weights); (2) lane_out reused rdx (A1q row) for corr1buf base, writing
  quant bytes into the correction table and leaving A1q zero (both INT8
  paths agreed vacuously; FP32-vs-INT8 caught it); (3) qb2v pointer-vs-
  value (stored b2f address, added pointer bits); (4) FNV is a hash.
- Live peabrain.db never touched (model/ + /tmp only). No GPU (Stage 5).

GPU (Stage 5: feasibility PROBE, 2026-11-04 — read-only recon, no devices
opened, no ioctls, no driver changes; verdict: NOT FEASIBLE under the hard
requirements, CPU remains backend of record).
Hardware/driver (all present, healthy): RTX 3060 GA106 LHR (01:00.0),
sm_86, 12GB (12288MiB), driver 610.57.04, kernel modules nvidia/nvidia_uvm/
nvidia_modeset/nvidia_drm loaded, nodes /dev/nvidia0+nvidiactl+nvidia-uvm
(+tools)+nvidia-modeset all 0666, DRM renderD128 present. nvidia.ko license
Dual MIT/GPL (open kernel modules flavor).
Routes examined and why each is blocked:
(a) libcuda.so.1 (EXISTS, 112MB, CUDA Driver API + PTX JIT for sm_86):
the sane route, HARD-BANNED (no libcuda, no shared libs, no dynamic deps).
(b) NVML: same ban; mgmt-only anyway.
(c) Direct /dev/nvidia* ioctls with hand-written userspace: the ioctl ABI
is proprietary/undocumented; open kernel sources publish numbers but the
working protocol (GSP-RPC sequences, channel/VASpace choreography,
per-engine pushbuffer methods, UVM fault handling, runlist submit) is the
multi-hundred-KLOC libcuda+firmware stack. Reimplementing it without
guessing layouts (banned) or destabilising the shared box is infeasible;
validating it would require the interfaces it replaces.
(d) Nouveau/DRM/NVK: proprietary driver owns the GPU (rebind = operational
change to shared homer); Nouveau Ampere is bring-up-grade (no reclocking,
fractional clocks) even if bound. Out, technically and operationally.
(e) Vulkan compute: needs Nouveau (see d) or libvulkan (banned, same as a).
Revisit ONLY if: requirements relax to dlopen-libcuda-with-fallback, or a
stable documented low-level compute ABI appears. Stated plainly: at current
model scale (65 params) the GPU buys nothing; revisit at millions of
embedding dims. model_status reports CPU backend + GPU-unavailable reason.
NO GPU CLAIM MADE (no kernel executed, per the rule). Stage 6 stays shut.

