Stage 6c (memory mapping: HARD GATE FOUND, work suspended for direction):
Alloc side PROVEN (C, repeated): NV01_MEMORY_LOCAL_USER (0x40) alloc/
free under device/subdevice with NVOS02 params, explicit handles,
any tested flags; subdevice (0x2080) + channel-group (0xa06c, zeroed
params) also alloc cleanly. Mapping side BLOCKED on every route tried:
 - classic RmMapMemory (0x21/XFER, NVOS33 exact per header): EINVAL x12
   variants (both fds, subdevice, sizes 44/48, flags 0/0x4000). Modern
   libcuda issues ZERO XFER ioctls: the classic RMAPI-via-XFER path is
   dead on 610.xx (rm_validate rejects it).
 - fd-mmap after alloc: no mapping context exists (EINVAL); contexts are
   created only by a successful map call (circular).
 - dma-buf export (17, published struct): EINVAL x14 (fds, types,
   parents, multi-object lists). Closed-RM dup gate; libcuda never uses
   it here (CUDA-IPC uses another mechanism).
 - UVM (libcuda-proven for transfers): INITIALIZE/PAGEABLE/CREATE_RANGE
   all succeed, but REGISTER_GPU fails 27 (INSUFFICIENT_PERMISSIONS)
   with byte-identical inputs to libcuda's succeeding call. Root cause:
   UVM GPU registration needs the vaspace/channel tree (libcuda owns
   channel-group 0xa06c + channels 0xc56f/0xc7c0/0xc7b5 + ctx-share
   0x9067 + events BEFORE registering; its hVaSpace IS a channel).
   Replicating that tree IS channel bring-up, i.e. 6d-adjacent work.
 - BAR static windows: none pre-registered (mmap fails).
UVM call ledger (bare ints on nvidia-uvm fds): INITIALIZE=0x30000001
(first op per fd, else later calls fail 22), MM_INIT=75 (two-fd bind
pattern observed), REGISTER_GPU=37, VASPACE=25, MAP_EXTERNAL=33
(needs registered GPU; attr {uuid,1,0,0,0,0} observed), plus 1/2/34/38
reserve/free/unregister. Full libcuda traffic map captured in session.
VERDICT: 6c-as-specified (memory before channels) is infeasible on this
driver: UVM mapping requires channel infrastructure. Options: (i) fold
channel-group/channel bring-up into 6c (merges with 6d-part), (ii) pause
memory until 6d builds channels first, (iii) accept 6c-partial (alloc/
free/sizes proven, mapping deferred). Awaiting operator direction.
Box left clean: ~50 test procs closed fds (kernel freed RM state),
smi shows pre-existing desktop only, 19W/41C baseline.

